<section class="how">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
    <h2>Ten commands become two.</h2>
    <div class="vs">
      <div class="col">
        <p class="lab">By hand</p>
        <pre><code><span>$</span> git worktree add ../myapp__worktrees/fix-login -b fix-login
<span>$</span> cp .env ../myapp__worktrees/fix-login/
<span>$</span> cd ../myapp__worktrees/fix-login
<span>$</span> tmux new-window -n fix-login
<span>$</span> tmux split-window -h "pnpm install && pnpm run dev"
<span>$</span> claude "Fix the login redirect"
<i># later</i>
<span>$</span> git checkout main && git merge fix-login
<span>$</span> git worktree remove ../myapp__worktrees/fix-login
<span>$</span> git branch -d fix-login
<span>$</span> tmux kill-window -t fix-login</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="col hi">
        <p class="lab">With workmux</p>
        <pre><code><span>$</span> workmux add fix-login -p "Fix the login redirect"
<i># later</i>
<span>$</span> workmux merge</code></pre>
        <ul class="perks">
          <li>
            Files to copy and panes to start come from <code>.workmux.yaml</code
            >
          </li>
          <li>Every agent's status shows in the sidebar and dashboard</li>
          <li>Repeat for as many tasks as you can keep up with</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="arrow" href="/guide/quick-start/">Quick start →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

